
Description:

Audit logging is now always enabled; the auditlog configuration option is
deprecated and has no effect.


Documentation:

None.


Config changes:

The auditlog option is deprecated and can be removed.  The audit log events
it used to gate are now always emitted.


Upgrade instructions:

Sites that did not previously enable auditlog will start seeing
"event=auditlog.*" entries in syslog, and should make sure their logging
setup is ready for the extra volume.  Consider limiting which syslog priorities
are logged.  Messages logged at "info" may be superfluous if you didn't want
the auditlog before.


GitHub issue:

None.
